You're right, I don't. But in *NETHACK* I would like one, not *on* me mind
you now but as part of the game interface...all i want is some sort of 
quantitative measure wrt to weights that would accurately inform the player
his ability to carry. at present the player is not allowed to carry the
next piece of item if that would incapacitate him. if he is fullup or nearly and
he successfully wished for a heavy item, success would add it to his inventory
but he cannot move,ie collapses...in my meter system, the meter would indicate
say 110% capacity, so the player know what and how much to discard in order to
keep the new item. at present there is much time wasting in trail and error
judgement to test carrying capacity while altering inventory.
...in order to accomodate the percentage weight system, items might have to be
listed not in absolute values,ie kgs. or lbs. but in percent of the whole...
...meaning Stormbringer is 2% of a player's carrying capacity of 100% and
so on...i suppose this would mean guess-work on types of bags is easier.
...but i think its better to count down then up...meaning that you start with
100% and as things are picked up this decreases until it reaches 0%. should
strenght be gain or lost the meter changes to eg.10% or -4%...now you can pick
that 4 arrows up or simply collapsed on the spot...

WRT food meter, I for one, can judge fairly well my hunger status, and how much
i can "pig-out" before i burst at the seams. I think choking is ok in the game
but it souldn't be a major health hazzard. Don't people throw-up if they ate too
much and get sick too? Perhaps this should be in the game? I said that realism
is not the strong point of the game, NOT meaning that it should be...the strong
point is FUN, and playability...i guess fun is subjective as most things are...

